{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"The `tool_loop` command orchestrates an autonomous development cycle by engaging an LLM in a recursive loop to solve complex tasks using available Newbound tools. It accepts a user `prompt`, executes a sequence of tool calls (reading, writing, compiling, verifying code), and handles debugging until a final result is achieved or a limit is reached. ROUND LIMIT: the agent's TOOL_BUDGET (runtime/agent/botd.properties, system.apps.agent.runtime) - the SAME knob the chat agentloop uses, read LIVE per call (floor 24, cap 1000), so the executive's reasoning and the chat agent share one setting. On budget exhaustion the model self-summarizes a resumable checkpoint (PROGRESS/NEXT/BLOCKERS) into final_answer prefixed '[budget checkpoint - incomplete, resume next turn]' so step_item can journal where it got to and the next drive tick resumes instead of restarting. Also aborts on repeated-identical-calls and 3 consecutive identical failures. Returns FLAT {msg, messages}.","import":"use flowlang::command::Command;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse crate::agent::llm::chat_llm::chat_llm;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\n","params":[{"name":"prompt","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"lnmvtl19edbeb72a7tc3a","readers":[],"time":1792520245272,"username":"system","writers":[]}